spans.s:
śaúr-ya, n. [śūra] heroism, valour, 🞄prowess: -karman, n. heroic deed;
 -rāśi, 🞄m. paragon of valour;
 -vat, a. heroic, valiant;
 🞄-sāgara, m. (ocean =) paragon of heroism;
 🞄-unmādin, a. foolhardy;
 -audārya-śṛṅgāra-maya, a. composed of heroism, nobility, 🞄and love of women.

saura, a. (ī) relating or belonging to, 🞄derived from, the sun (sūrya), solar;
 m. worshipper 🞄of the sun;
 son of the sun, planet 🞄Saturn;
 n. collection of hymns to the sun.

saurabh-a, a. [surabhi] fragrant;
 n. 🞄fragrance;
 (saúrabh) -eya, m. [Surabhi] bull: 🞄pl. (herd of) cattle: ī, f. (C.) (daughter of 🞄Surabhi), cow;
 -ya, n. fragrance, perfume;
 🞄(fig.) universal diffusion.
